---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About &amp; Methodology"
  description="Who writes Equity Drift, how the hand-data filters work, an honest note on sample sizes, and how affiliate links on this site are handled."
>
  <main class="about" id="main-content">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow mono">About this site</p>
      <h1>The person, the process, the caveats</h1>
      <p class="dek">
        Equity Drift is one player checking his own study habits against his own hand
        database, in public. Here's who's behind it, how the numbers are produced, and
        where those numbers fall short.
      </p>
    </section>

    <article class="panel">
      <h2>Who writes this</h2>
      <p>
        Equity Drift is written by Nate Armstrong, a regulated-market Pot-Limit Omaha
        player — micro-to-small-stakes, Ontario iGaming market. No coaching
        credentials, no claimed edge beyond what a given post's data actually shows.
        The site exists because tracking software makes it possible to check a study
        habit against reality instead of just trusting it, and because writing the
        check-up down is a more useful study method than doing it silently.
      </p>
      <p>
        This isn't a results-based brag site or a coaching funnel. When a mantra doesn't
        hold up, that's the post.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
      <h2>How the research works</h2>
      <p>
        Every post starts with a specific, falsifiable filter run against hand history
        logged in PokerTracker 4 — never a vibe or a memory of "how things usually go."
        The general shape:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Pick one specific study mantra or rule of thumb.</li>
        <li>Define a PT4 filter that isolates exactly the situation the mantra describes.</li>
        <li>Report what the filtered hands actually show, including when it contradicts the mantra.</li>
        <li>Pull a small number of representative hands to illustrate the pattern, not to cherry-pick the best-looking ones.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Because Ontario's regulated online market ring-fences each site's player pool
        (a structural liquidity constraint, not a bankroll one), a smooth stake ladder
        doesn't really exist here — PLO2 is well-populated, PLO5 is thin, and PLO10
        effectively doesn't run. Early posts draw on a combined PLO2/PLO5 dataset for
        that reason: it's the largest sample currently available, and it's used to prove
        out the filtering method itself while volume builds at higher stakes. Posts will
        move to higher-stakes data as specific findings call for it, and any post drawing
        on a different stake mix says so.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel callout">
      <h2>A note on sample sizes</h2>
      <p>
        Poker numbers over small samples are noisy, and this site's numbers are often
        small. A post built on 54 hands is a real, honestly-run check — it is not a
        statistically reliable win rate, and it should not be read as one. Where a
        finding is based on fewer hands than you'd want for confidence, that will be
        stated in the post rather than left for you to guess at from the stats sidebar.
      </p>
      <p>
        Nothing on this site is financial advice, a guarantee of results, or a substitute
        for your own bankroll and risk decisions. Treat each post as a documented
        experiment on one player's data, not as a universal strategy claim.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="panel">
      <h2>Affiliate disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Some links on this site may be affiliate or rakeback-partner links, meaning
        Equity Drift could earn a commission or rake-back share if you sign up or play
        through them, at no extra cost to you. Any such link will be labelled as such
        near where it appears. Affiliate relationships never determine what a post
        concludes — the data is pulled and reported the same way whether or not a link
        happens to be nearby, and a mantra that fails its own test gets reported as
        failing regardless of who might advertise here.
      </p>
      <p>
        As of this writing, no affiliate links are live on this site. This page will be
        kept current if and when that changes.
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- TODO: add a contact line here once the domain mail relay is set up
         (e.g. "Questions or corrections? Email nate@equitydriftpoker.ca").
         Deliberately not linking to the GitHub repo publicly. -->
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { max-width: 50rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 4rem 1.5rem 5rem; }

  .hero { padding: 2.75rem clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3.5rem) 1.5rem; }
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--cyan); margin: 0 0 0.9rem; font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', monospace;
  }
  .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.8rem); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .dek { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.1rem; max-width: 38rem; }

  .panel {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--felt-line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 2rem clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    margin: 0 1.5rem 1.5rem;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 70px -30px rgba(4, 2, 10, 0.75);
  }
  .panel h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .panel p, .panel li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .panel p + p { margin-top: 1rem; }
  .panel ol {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
  }
  .panel ol li + li { margin-top: 0.4rem; }

  /* The sample-size note gets the same gold-edged treatment as inline
     stat callouts in posts, so its caution reads as a design signal too */
  .panel.callout {
    border: 1px solid rgba(232, 178, 63, 0.35);
    background: rgba(9, 6, 18, 0.4);
  }
  .panel.callout h2 { color: var(--gold); }

  .contact {
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 48rem) {
    .about { padding: 2.5rem 0 3.5rem; }
    .hero { padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem; }
    .panel { margin: 0 1rem 1.25rem; padding: 1.5rem 1.25rem; }
    .contact { padding: 0 1.25rem; }
  }
</style>
